# Store listing — public legal URLs

When the user works on **App Store**, **Google Play**, **store listing**, **EAS submit**, **app review**, or asks about publishing / going live:

## Remind them

Terms and Privacy currently live **in-app only**. Stores need **public https URLs**.

Owner plan (do not invent a website):

1. Remind: “For store submission, generate shareable Google Docs (or Notion) for Terms and Privacy from `src/constants/legalTerms.ts` and `src/constants/legalPrivacy.ts`.”
2. Offer to draft the full doc text from those files when they are ready.
3. After they create public “anyone with the link” URLs, wire them into store listings (and optionally Settings / legal screens).

## Do not

- Invent fake domains or claim a website exists.
- Name the individual publisher in legal copy unless they explicitly ask (operator is “LyVee Labs” as an individual; contact `lyveelabs@gmail.com`; Texas / Harris County).
